### LMS Authentication Flow Tests
### Works with IntelliJ HTTP Client or VS Code REST Client.
### Make sure your app is running on localhost:8080.
###
### Notes:
### - These tests assume your auth controller uses: /api/auth
### - The login endpoint should create a session cookie, usually JSESSIONID.
### - IntelliJ HTTP Client and VS Code REST Client usually keep cookies between requests
###   for the same host, so logout can use the session created by login.
### - If you re-run duplicate tests with fixed emails, old database rows may make
###   the first request fail too. Change the email variables if needed.

@host = http://localhost:8080

@studentEmail = student-auth-flow@example.com
@teacherEmail = teacher-auth-flow@example.com
@duplicateEmail = duplicate-auth-flow@example.com
@studentPassword = Password123!
@teacherPassword = Password123!
@wrongPassword = WrongPassword123!

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Register a new student
### Expected:
### - 200 OK
### - Response should include id, firstName, lastName, email, accountStatus, roles
### - Response should NOT include passwordHash
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register/student
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Student",
  "lastName": "AuthFlow",
  "email": "{{studentEmail}}",
  "password": "{{studentPassword}}"
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Register a new teacher
### Expected:
### - 200 OK
### - roles should include TEACHER
### Warning:
### - Public teacher registration is okay for testing, but should probably become
###   invite-only or admin-approved later.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register/teacher
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Teacher",
  "lastName": "AuthFlow",
  "email": "{{teacherEmail}}",
  "password": "{{teacherPassword}}"
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Duplicate email setup
### First request should succeed unless this email already exists in your DB.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register/student
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Duplicate",
  "lastName": "One",
  "email": "{{duplicateEmail}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Duplicate email attempt
### Expected:
### - 400 Bad Request
### - Response should include: Email is already in use.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register/student
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Duplicate",
  "lastName": "Two",
  "email": "{{duplicateEmail}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Register with invalid email
### Expected:
### - 400 Bad Request
### - Response should include email validation message.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register/student
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Invalid",
  "lastName": "Email",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Register with short password
### Expected:
### - 400 Bad Request
### - Response should include password validation message.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register/student
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Short",
  "lastName": "Password",
  "email": "short-password-auth-flow@example.com",
  "password": "123"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Test current user before login
### Expected:
### - 401 Unauthorized
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. Login with wrong password
### Expected:
### - 401 Unauthorized
### - Response should include: Invalid email or password.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{studentEmail}}",
  "password": "{{wrongPassword}}"
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. Login with student credentials
### Expected:
### - 200 OK
### - Response should be UserResponse
### - Response should NOT include passwordHash
### - Response headers should include Set-Cookie: JSESSIONID=...
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{studentEmail}}",
  "password": "{{studentPassword}}"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Get current user from active session
### Expected:
### - 200 OK
### - Response should be UserResponse
### - Confirms JSESSIONID session can restore logged-in user
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 9. Login with teacher credentials
### Expected:
### - 200 OK
### - roles should include TEACHER
### - This may replace the previous session cookie depending on your REST client.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{teacherEmail}}",
  "password": "{{teacherPassword}}"
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 10. Logout
### Expected:
### - Usually 200, 204, or 302 depending on your Spring Security logout config.
### - Should invalidate the current session and delete/expire JSESSIONID.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Test current user after logout
### Expected:
### - 401 Unauthorized
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 11. Login after logout to confirm credentials still work
### Expected:
### - 200 OK
### - New session cookie.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{studentEmail}}",
  "password": "{{studentPassword}}"
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Optional protected endpoint test
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Use this after you create a protected endpoint, for example:
###
### @protectedUrl = {{host}}/api/courses
###
### GET {{protectedUrl}}
###
### Expected before login:
### - 401 Unauthorized
###
### Expected after login:
### - 200 OK, 403 Forbidden, or app-specific response depending on user role.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
